From 719b0e69095d44056fe6b5da05e4f5f10871a5b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GEN <gen@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:00:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] GEN: the full-drum Risograph look, the power-on default

A RISO palette (paper, black, dense orange, pink; passes the 4.5:1 gate) and a
third STYLE, RISO: every box a printed one, 2 px ink outline with a 1 px shadow
in the next ink a pixel off; the four knob cards on every page in their own inks,
the GEN layer's rows likewise, the lanes on a yellow block with green knockouts,
lit cells solid ink with paper text (gfx.c UI_RISO_INK, ux_pen). A fresh start
boots into it (panel.c settings_init, ui.c style_fresh); stored as STYLE 3.
tests: the renderer draws every screen in RISO (0 lint findings), the UI suite
covers the new palette, the three styles and the fresh-start path; docs/riso/.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UKiQQaFAeD8B44b8duY1gJ
