From 71c08bff7dcc45248537c437396c6519e243af98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:23:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] GEN: Turing registers, learned Markov chains,
 logistic-map chaos, pink dice, cross-track CALL, BREED, trig conditions

The techniques of the generative-music notes: a Turing-machine shift register
(FLIP 0 a locked loop) on DRUMS, CHORDS and LEAD, run on by LIVE a cycle a bar;
MARKOV melodies for BASS and LEAD whose table blends a seeded interval
preference with one learned from the track as the layer opened (black key 10
LEARN); CHAOS, the logistic map, periodic to chaotic by R; PINK, Voss-McCartney
1/f dice; CALL, cross-track logic against the kick, snare, any drum, bass or
lead, with NOT; BREED on black key 9, a bitwise crossover of this roll's seeds
and the previous one's; varied quiet drum steps take Felucca's trig conditions.
Render order DRUMS, BASS, CHORDS, LEAD so CALL reads this phrase. GEN_METHODS_MAX
9; the store layout is unchanged. Tests: register lock / flip, 8-step loops,
CALL NOT KICK, learned alternation, BREED crossover, conditions; UI keys and
method names. GEN.md updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UKiQQaFAeD8B44b8duY1gJ
